  "notes": [
    "These profiler runs are separate from native timing repetitions.",
    "Nsight Systems uses three accepted MNIST images (3000 steps); Brunel uses 100 ms warmup plus 50 ms measured.",
    "Kernel durations include GPU execution overhead, memory stalls and idle lanes; they are not pure arithmetic time.",
    "CPU launch durations overlap GPU execution and cannot be subtracted from wall time as an independent component.",
    "NCU samples 30 matching launches after skipping 900 matching launches; clocks and caches are not controlled.",
    "The short Brunel profile covers the first 50 ms after warmup, not the complete 1000 ms baseline interval. Its averages are activity-dependent and are not substitutes for the baseline.",
    "No explicit Synchronize API calls occur inside the selected kernel span. Synchronous memcpy operations at presentation boundaries still wait for device completion.",
    "The first NCU attempt hit a lock owned elsewhere in /tmp; successful ncub runs used a private TMPDIR under the task directory."
